  "content": {
    "title": "Houston vs Texas A&M score, results: Cougars into March Madness Sweet 16",
    "text": "Updated March 21, 2026, 9:03 p.m. ETFollow all of Saturday's NCAA Tournament second round games with USA TODAY Sports' live updates.Houston, we don't have a problem.The Cougars are in formation and will advance to Sweet 16 round after the No. 2 seed put on a dominant showcase against the No. 10-seed Texas A&M Aggies, obliterating them, 88-57, in the Second Round of the NCAA men's basketball tournament at Paycom Center in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma.As a team, they overcame a 26% shooting performance from three-point territory. They were all over the glass, outrebounding the Aggies, 46-29. The disparity on the offensive boards was most glaring, the Cougars grabbed 19 offensive rebounds, compared to Texas A&M's nine. It resulted in Houston dominating the paint, outscoring the Aggies 32-20 down low.Defensively, they clamped the Aggies, having 11 forced turnovers and seven blocked shots.Four players scored in double-digits for the Cougars, led by senior guard Emanuel Sharp with 18. Freshman sensation Kingston Flemings score nine points after a tough shooting night, going 4-of-10.The Aggies were led by junior guard Josh Holloway who scored 12 off the bench. No Aggie starter scored double-digits. As a team, they were held to 35% shooting, including 25% from deep. Their biggest deficit was 31. Texas A&M finishes the season with a 22-12 record.The Cougars will go back home for the next round as the South region Sweet 16 games are played at Toyota Center in Houston, Texas.They will face the winner between No. 3-seed Illinois and No. 11-seed VCU.Here's what you need to know from Saturday's second round game with highlights and results: Final: No. 2 Houston 88, No. 10 Texas A&M 57No. 2-seed Houston Cougars advance to the Sweet 16 after defeating the No. 10-seed Texas A&M Aggies, 88-57, at Paycom Center in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma on March 21.The Cougars were led by senior guard Emanuel Sharp who scored 18 points. Fellow senior Milos Uzan added 15. Freshmen Chris Cenac Jr. scored 17, while Mercy Miller, the son of rapper, entrepreneur and former NBA player Percy \"Master P\" Miller, scored 12 off the bench. Attack of the Cougars continuesHouston came out of the locker room in the second half and continued where they left off.They started on a 6-0 run, as Flemings started to come alive in the contest. The second half was all Houston as they extended their double-digit lead into a blowout growing their largest lead to 28.Unless a miracle occurs, the No. 2-seed Houston Cougars will advance to the Sweet 16 Round. Halftime: No. 2 Houston 46, No. 10 Texas A&M 28No. 2-seed Houston pulled away around the midway point of the first half after both teams matched each other's intensity going point-for-point.What began as a close neck game, has separated to a glaring difference in programs. The Cougars took advantage of havoc-wrecking defense to go on a 21-4 run in a 10-minute span to end the half.The outlier is on the offensive rebounds. Houston outrebounded Texas A&M on the offensive glass, 11-7. Additionally, they forced seven first half turnovers, which turned into easy offense for the Cougars.Houston is led by senior guard Emanuel Sharp with 14 first half points on 4-of-9 shooting. Freshman Chris Cenac Jr. added 10. Fellow freshman Kingston Flemings got off to slow start but had six in the first half. The Aggies have seven scoring players in first 20 minutes. Back-and-forth affair in battle of Southeast TexasThe Second Round of the NCAA Tournament between No. 2-seed Houston and No. 10-seed Texas A&M has been a even-skilled battle at Paycom Center in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma.The Cougars have a slim, 17-13, lead with 10:53 left in the first half. What's been working for Houston is the valiant effort on the boards, outrebounding the Aggies, 12-6, early in the game. Emanuel Sharp leads the way with eight points for Houston.Aggies have five players register a point so far in this contest. But tempers began to flare causing Texas A&M to lose their cool.The Aggies coaching staff felt a call was missed and the bench was assessed a technical foul. Just about a minute later, Rubén Dominguez committed a Flagrant Foul 1 when attempting to get through a screen with under 10 minutes in the first half.It helped to spark a Cougar run and they extended their lead to 23-16. But the Aggies would respond behind a Josh Holloway 25-foot three-point jumper, followed by a Rashaun Agee layup from Holloway.The lead was four in favor of Houston, 25-21, with 8:37 left in the half. Cougars lost Chase McCarty to injury with 6:37 in the first half. He went diving for a loose ball and had other players land on him. He came up limping, hobbling on one leg. He would later return.Houston played stifling defense, thanks to two big blocks at the rim from Joseph Tugler. It helped lead to easy offense, as the Cougars saw their lead grow to 11 with 4:16 left. Texas A&M has missed nine-consecutive field goals, as Houston went on a 16-0 run. The Cougs built a 17-point lead, 41-24, with 1:18 in the first half.Pop Isaacs ended the run with two free throws, but Houston would end the half with a 18-point lead, following a six-minute scoring drought by the Aggies. Houston vs Texas A&M live scoreTEAMS1H2HFTexas A&M282957Houston464288What time is Houston vs Texas A&M?Time: 6:10 p.m. ET, Saturday.What channel is Houston vs Texas A&M? How to watch, streaming infoThe game is airing on TNT, streaming via Fubo.Houston vs Texas A&M prediction, oddsEhsan Kassim: Texas A&MJordan Mendoza: HoustonJohn Leuzzi: HoustonBlake Schuster: HoustonMoneyline: Houston (-500); Texas A&M (+375)Spread: Houston (-10.5)Over/under total: 143.5Kingston Flemings 2026 NBA Draft predictionUtah Jazz at No. 5 overall.Kalbrosky's Analysis:The Jazz currently have the worst defensive rating in the league but could potentially improve that by selecting Houston freshman Kingston Flemings. The All-Big 12 guard has several games when he has recorded at least three steals, notching eight against Arizona State earlier this season. He scored 42 points against No. 11 Texas Tech on Jan. 24 and had a strong performance against Baylor, recording 21 points with seven assists and two steals on March 4. With highs as high as his thus far, it will not take long for him to hear his name called on draft night.See USA TODAY's full mock draft here.Kingston Flemings stats(all stats as of March 15)16.4 points per game3.9 rebounds per game5.3 assists per game47.5% field goal percentage39.2% three-point field goal percentageHouston NCAA Tournament history (since 2014)Appearances: 7Most recent appearance: 2025Games played: 26 (19-6)Highest seed: 1Lowest seed: 6Best finish: National Championship",
